\loch\hich\dbch\pard\plain\ltrpar\itap0{\lang1033\fs30\f2\cf0 \cf0\ql{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch This dialog adds Thoughts and Links to the Universal Knowledge Store (UKS) which is a graph of Thoughts.  Each Link consists of a Source Thought, a Target Thought, and a LinkType Thought.  Enter Thought labels into the Source, Type, and Target boxes and press Add/Update to create a link.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Example}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Source: Fido}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Type: is-a}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Target: dog}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Would indicate that Fido is a dog. This is shown in the UKS dialog as a parent/child Link.  All other link types are shown as Source->Type->Target. All words in labels are singularized so:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Source: dogs}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Type: have}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Target: fur}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Is shown as dog->has->fur.  In general, Thoughts in the UKS represent abstract singular entities so the Link dog->has.4->leg would represent that all dogs have 4 legs.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch If the Thoughts in the text boxes do not exist, the boxes will have a yellow background and the Thoughts will be created. If the link already exists, no action will be taken. In some cases the target may be omitted as in Mary runs. If a label is entered with an asterisk, it will have digits appended to it to ensure that it is unique. This feature can be used to create sequences in a specific order as in Pi->hasDigit*->3,  Pi->hasDigit*->., Pi->hasDigit*->1,  Pi->hasDigit*->4.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs40\f4 {\cf2\ltrch Subclasses}\li0\ri0\sa80\sb360\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Putting multiple labels in the text boxes will create a subclass. }\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Example:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Source: Fido}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Type: is-a}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Target: big dog}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Will create a subclass of dog, big.dog with the Link big.dog->is->big and make Fido a child of big.dog.  In the Source and Target boxes, modifiers precede the main Thought; in the Type box, modifiers follow the type. }\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Example:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Source: Mary}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Type: can play}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Target: electric violin}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Where the Target creates a subclass of violin with the modifier electric, the Type creates a subclass of can with the modifier play.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs40\f4 {\cf2\ltrch Sequences}\li0\ri0\sa80\sb360\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Sequences can be entered by prefacing the sequence with a "^" character and putting spaces between the Value thought labels.  }\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Example:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Source: Fido}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Type: spelled}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Target: ^F i d o}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs40\f4 {\cf2\ltrch Conditionals}\li0\ri0\sa80\sb360\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Compound and Conditional statements can be created by putting a simple statement in either the Source or Target boxes.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Example:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Source: Fido plays outside}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Type: if}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Target: weather is sunny}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch This will automatically create labels for the compound links (e.g. R0, R1...)  These can be used to reference these relationships later to create more complex links:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Example:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Source: R0}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Type: when}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Target: R1}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs28\f3 {\ltrch Link may also have a confidence level and a time-to-live which will be set if the Set Confidence/TTL checkbox is checked. Confidences can change automatically under certain conditions. When the timeToLive of a Link expires, it will vanish. If this is an "Event", that is, part of a sequence, checking the "This is an Event" checkbox will also add this statement to an event queue.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
}
}

