\loch\hich\dbch\pard\plain\ltrpar\itap0{\lang1033\fs30\f2\cf0 \cf0\ql{\fs40\f3 {\cf2\ltrch Sound Output}\li0\ri0\sa80\sb360\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch This module can play stored musical phrases.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch The }{\b\ltrch Play Sound}{\ltrch  button is provided only to verify that the computer\rquote s sound system is working. It is not part of the learning or action process.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch Stored phrases can be played using the system\rquote s internal representation. The }{\b\ltrch cadence}{\ltrch  and }{\b\ltrch pitch offset}{\ltrch  controls demonstrate that these phrases are not tied to absolute pitch or timing.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch Instead, phrases are represented as sequences in a way that is largely:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\b\ltrch pitch-independent}{\ltrch  (can be shifted up or down)}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\b\ltrch speed-independent}{\ltrch  (can be played faster or slower)}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch This reflects how sequences are stored structurally rather than as fixed audio signals.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
}
}

