\loch\hich\dbch\pard\plain\ltrpar\itap0{\lang1033\fs30\f2\cf0 \cf0\ql{\fs40\f3 {\cf2\ltrch Sound Input}\li0\ri0\sa80\sb360\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch This module allows you to input musical phrases using the computer keyboard or by entering a stored phrase name.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch The dialog text shows how the lower two rows of the keyboard map to piano keys (white and black keys). There is a slight delay between keystrokes and the sound.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch When you play a sequence of notes:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch The system stores it as a phrase with a short time-to-live (TTL)}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch Repeating the phrase strengthens it and extends its lifetime}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch If you enter part of a known phrase, the system may }{\b\ltrch complete the phrase}{\ltrch  automatically based on what it has learned.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch If you enter a complete phrase, the system treats it as a recognized input and may:}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch select a response phrase}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\pntext \'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart1{\pntxtb\'B7}}{\ltrch play that response}\li720\ri0\sa160\sb0\jclisttab\tx720\fi-360\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch If the response leads to an increase in well-being, the association between the input and response is strengthened, making that response more likely in the future.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 {\ltrch You can also type the name of a stored phrase into the textbox. The system will behave as if it has just heard that phrase as input.}\li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
{\fs24\f4 \li0\ri0\sa160\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
}
}

